Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: keel-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: GnuPG archive key of the Keel Linux package repository
 The OpenPGP public key that signs the Release files of the Keel Linux
 archive, installed as /usr/share/keyrings/keel-archive-keyring.gpg for
 the Signed-By field of an apt source, with the armored copy and the
 fingerprint of the primary key beside it.
 .
 The package installs the key and nothing else. It does not add an apt
 source, does not change apt's configuration and has no maintainer
 script: enabling the archive is keel-transition's job, and it is a
 separate decision.
